30,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My observations confirm a congestion problem. People are shifting bikes to get out, which is inefficient and risks damage.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The financial records show that we have very little flexibility. Any new infrastructure would require a direct levy on the residents.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,It seems my suspicions were correct. The same flats have held the best spots for years without any formal review.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,How predictable. The neighbors tried a fee system and it just made people stop talking to each other. Not a great precedent.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,I found out that the paperwork is actually a bit of a pain! And those display frames look tricky to use.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, if a levy is necessary to prevent damage to property, it's a logical expense. The current chaos is unsustainable.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,A levy is a hard sell. We need to know if the residents are willing to pay for a more organized system.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,The fact that there has been no review for five years is the core of the resentment. We cannot ignore the lack of fairness.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Fairness is a slippery slope. If we start auditing who ""deserves"" a spot, we'll have people timing their exits to avoid their neighbors.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, if we get fancy frames, someone has to grease them! I don't want us to just forget about it after a month.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, maintenance is a separate issue. The priority is the physical bottleneck. We need a system that prioritizes flow over tenure.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,I am concerned that we are ignoring the cost of administration. Adding per-place billing increases the treasurer's workload significantly.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"I believe we should consider a rotation or a lottery. The current ""first-come, first-served"" from five years ago is no longer valid.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,A lottery is a gamble with social harmony. I'd prefer a solution that doesn't turn the lobby into a courtroom.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"But that's my point! If the treasurer is already stressed, adding more billing will just make them quit. We need something simple!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"Simplicity is good, but not at the cost of functionality. We must address the ""shoving match"" occurring every morning.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will support any option that minimizes unexpected costs to the building account and doesn't create an administrative nightmare.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,I will support a change that breaks the cycle of the same people holding the same spots. Transparency is key here.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Just keep in mind that ""transparency"" often looks like a public shaming list. Let's keep the peace, shall we?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,I just want to make sure we don't create a job that nobody wants to do. Let's pick the easiest one to maintain!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
